There are $90$ teeth in the whole, and we're thinking about $9$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{9}{90}
&=\dfrac{1}{10} \cdot \dfrac{9}{9}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{10}
\end{align}$

There are $90$ teeth in the whole, and we're thinking about $27$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{27}{90}
&=\dfrac{3}{10} \cdot \dfrac{9}{9}\\\\
&=\dfrac{3}{10}
\end{align}$
